      "note": [
        "Statistics Sweden conducts data collection in accordance to the Eurostat manual ”Environmental goods and services sector accounts - Handbook” (2016). It describes which environmental areas, industries and variables (e.g. output and export) to include. Environmental Goods and Services Sector is commonly abbreviated using the letters EGSS.\r\n\r\nStatistics Sweden follows the Eurostat and EU definition of EGSS. EU regulation 691/2011 describes EGSS as the production activities of a national economy that generate environmental products for the purpose of environmental protection and resource management. Resource management includes the preservation, maintenance and enhancement of the stock of natural resources and therefore the safeguarding of those resources against depletion.",
        "2022-12-14 correction of net turnover in industry A02, F41 and for Totals.",
        "The source of net turnover in the Environmental Goods and Services Sector (EGSS) is the Structural Business Statistics."
      ],
